Screen:
| nice_cpu      V9.9                            the 32-bit NICE CPU of B. Ulmann
| F1 typewriter   F3 key codes   F5 charset   F7 counters   F9 comet   F11 board
|
|  Since reset, while the core runs
|
|    Time, h:mm:ss.hh                              0:00:00.08
|    Microseconds                                       80053
|    Cycles                                             80055
|    Instructions                                       80057
|    Clock in MHz, cycles per microsecond                   1
|
|  A prime sieve to 2048, run before each update
|    Runs                                                   2
|    Primes found                                         309
|    Instructions                                       30058
|    Cycles                                             30058
|    Microseconds                                       30058
|    Cycles per instruction                              1.00
|    Instructions per microsecond                        1.00
|
|  On a board, the time is real, and the clock is that of the core.
|  In niceemu, each step counts as a cycle and as a microsecond.
